                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most outré"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "561c0a16-eee3-31b9-8405-b1951894e112",
                        "entry_id": "62336912-edd3-36aa-9563-794a34979a84",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Beyond what is customary or proper; extravagant."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "07ea8115-eefb-41a0-b31a-ade7e8621aa0",
                                "sense_id": "561c0a16-eee3-31b9-8405-b1951894e112",
                                "text": "I believe I have been very rude; but really Miss Fairfax has done her hair in so odd a way—so very odd a way—that I cannot keep my eyes from her. I never saw any thing so outrée!—Those curls!—This must be a fancy of her own. I see nobody else looking like her!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "030e57cc-e637-4127-a89b-92aeb3e5e663",
                                "sense_id": "561c0a16-eee3-31b9-8405-b1951894e112",
                                "text": "He hated people who did not know where to stop. Ernest was always so outré and strange; there was never any knowing what he would do next, except that it would be something unusual and silly."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "86d64666-a4d5-42b8-a175-266253f81cd1",
                                "sense_id": "561c0a16-eee3-31b9-8405-b1951894e112",
                                "text": "Her career as a performer, a model and a high priestess of the outré has been rooted for decades in catwalk-Kabuki mischief and provocation."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f0db8cbd-ef59-48af-851d-ab45793e2ba9",
                                "sense_id": "561c0a16-eee3-31b9-8405-b1951894e112",
                                "text": "Are his patrons simply too giddy in this post-pandemic moment to muster sustained outrage over his outré behavior?"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "1b22a122-5eb4-3d86-a0f4-0866aa04b626",
                        "entry_id": "62336912-edd3-36aa-9563-794a34979a84",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Very unconventional."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "dc674e6f-448e-4108-b8ef-f4697b9376b8",
                                "sense_id": "1b22a122-5eb4-3d86-a0f4-0866aa04b626",
                                "text": "1992, David Littlejohn, The Ultimate Art: Essays Around and About Opera, Chapter 16: The Twentieth Century Takes on Shakespeare, page 261,\nTo begin with, King Lear is the most unconventional, the most nearly hysterical, the most outré and outrageous play Shakespeare ever wrote."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "52f01d0f-b4ca-4c9d-936c-4923e3290127",
